  <h2>What the numbers look like</h2>
  <p>A quick, conservative sketch, not a promise. At about $1,500 a month in ad spend, registrations in a niche like this tend to run in the low teens each, so figure on the order of a hundred-plus parents registering a month. Typically about 30% show up live. If a conservative 8 to 12% of those join the Club at $67 a month, that is a handful of new members every month, and because the Club is a membership they stack: the same always-on funnel that adds four or five members in month one is adding to a base that keeps paying in month six. The $37 workshops convert a further slice on top. Every figure here is an industry benchmark, not your data, and nothing is guaranteed.</p>

